{"version":"1","id":"surma","handle":"surma","name":"Surma","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/5d6f8bb8b7584f54acf7d242d7c08834","description":null,"is_squad":false,"x":-4.1655,"y":3.4617,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":11,"newest_post_at":"2025-06-17T16:41:21.091Z","oldest_post_at":"2021-01-15T00:00:00.000Z","features":{"hype_score":0.0,"listicle_ratio":0.0,"question_ratio":0.090909,"avg_read_time":15.111111,"summary_length_avg":330.090909,"title_length_avg":50.545455,"title_length_var":101.702479,"tag_entropy":2.664532,"tag_diversity":1.545455,"top_tag_share":0.090909,"avg_upvotes":5.454545,"median_upvotes":2.0,"avg_comments":0.272727,"comment_to_upvote_ratio":0.065574,"zero_engagement_share":0.272727,"viral_share":0.0,"posts_per_week":0.04898,"non_article_ratio":0.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"recency_skew":0.1},"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[4.8824,4.3971],"cadence_depth":[-9.6471,8.0],"hype_variety":[-4.7941,-5.1176],"title_style":[8.5735,-1.75]},"top_tags":[["webdev",4],["javascript",3],["webassembly",3],["general-programming",3],["automation",1],["langchain",1],["langgraph",1],["llm",1]],"sample_titles":{"representative":["LangGraph for complex workflows \u2014 surma.dev","The cost of convenience \u2014 surma.dev","Rust to WebAssembly the hard way \u2014 surma.dev"],"outlier":["My approach to coding interviews: Optimize for iteration \u2014 surma.dev"]},"recent_posts":[{"id":"6yPhFxYMU","title":"LangGraph for complex workflows \u2014 surma.dev","url":"https://surma.dev/things/langgraph/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/langgraph-for-complex-workflows-surma-dev-6yphfxymu","summary":"LangGraph enables building complex workflow architectures with cyclic patterns that LangChain's DAG-based approach cannot handle. The library supports local LLM orchestration, agent clusters, and multi-step automations through graph-based state management. Key features include structured responses, tool integration, conditional edges for loops, and parallel node execution with reducers for state reconciliation. The tutorial demonstrates building ReAct agents that can perform multi-step reasoning and tool invocation cycles.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/75e71b87488222c22bdb627796b9c424?_a=AQAEulh","num_upvotes":16,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-06-17T16:41:21.091Z"},{"id":"RiXGXPZUf","title":"[Video] Nix explained from the ground up \u2014 surma.dev","url":"https://surma.dev/things/nix-explained/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/video-nix-explained-from-the-ground-up-surma-dev-rixgxpzuf","summary":"The post introduces Nix, explaining its functionality. The author has shared a video to provide an in-depth explanation and is considering making similar videos in the future.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/9c6ecb56c1b2c15e5df0b0129f9b5232?_a=AQAEuiZ","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-09-06T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"IsFfcpQvh","title":"Rust to WebAssembly the hard way \u2014 surma.dev","url":"https://surma.dev/things/rust-to-webassembly/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/rust-to-webassembly-the-hard-way-surma-dev-isffcpqvh","summary":"In Rust, the tool that makes WebAssembly easy is called wasm-bindgen, and we are going to ditch it! At the same time, Rust is a bit different in that WebAssembly has been a first-class target for a long time and the standard library is laid out to support it out of the box.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/6fe46a8b1438827274a545412062c241","num_upvotes":10,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-02-13T16:39:51.337Z"},{"id":"N4Emu8Qmd","title":"I turned JS into a compiled language (for fun and Wasm) \u2014 surma.dev","url":"https://surma.dev/things/compile-js/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/i-turned-js-into-a-compiled-language-for-fun-and-wasm-surma-dev-n4emu8qmd","summary":"JavaScript looks a lot like C++, but C++20 has to offer as well as JavaScript. The program is nonsense, of course, but it covers a good range of features that I want to support. Be warned, though: This is the first time I\u2019m using C ++20.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/330fde3d7ceb86c043d2c32e4a0e5d6f","num_upvotes":9,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-10-03T12:17:24.305Z"},{"id":"0K8Zuj_QE","title":"The cost of convenience \u2014 surma.dev","url":"https://surma.dev/things/cost-of-convenience/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/the-cost-of-convenience-surma-dev-0k8zuj-qe","summary":"The Web Platform is a beautiful mess. It has been expanded and evolved by hundreds (thousands?) of people over the last couple of decades. Some APIs on the Web Platform are decades old, while others barely have a couple of months under their belt. The web is uneven across at least three dimensions: Level of abstraction, API design and availability/behavior.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/3ca28ac781fcec6ef0e2574fe47178dc","num_upvotes":13,"num_comments":1,"created_at":"2022-06-17T10:51:44.868Z"},{"id":"qdEY0ykx6","title":"DOM2Texture: Abusing Arcane APIs \u2014 surma.dev","url":"https://surma.dev/things/dom2texture/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/dom2texture-abusing-arcane-apis-surma-dev-qdey0ykx6","summary":"When using WebGL, you have to do everything yourself, including font rendering and layouting. I thought: \u201cWouldn\u2019t it be great if you could just reuse the browser\u2019s layouting and font-rendering engine instead of heaving to reinvent the wheel?\u201d Yes, but there's no API for that. Or is there?TL;DR: You can use <foreignObject> to embed normal HTML content in an SVG.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/9596569d07b91ff27b5d63809bcc48d9","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-04-02T08:40:03.297Z"},{"id":"DAmxVm16L","title":"WebGPU \u2014 All of the cores, none of the canvas \u2014 surma.dev","url":"https://surma.dev/things/webgpu/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/webgpu-all-of-the-cores-none-of-the-canvas-surma-dev-damxvm16l","summary":"WebGPU is an upcoming Web API that gives you low-level, general-purpose access to GPUs. The goal for this blog post is to make WebGPU accessible for web developers. I won\u2019t use WebGPU to generate graphics. Instead, I will use Web GPU to access the raw computing power a GPU provides.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/80fe49aa1b0b3f4f4b9784058ba3fdf5","num_upvotes":7,"num_comments":2,"created_at":"2022-03-08T13:29:46.341Z"},{"id":"SPzhRfLx6","title":"My approach to coding interviews: Optimize for iteration \u2014 surma.dev","url":"https://surma.dev/things/spreadsheet/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/my-approach-to-coding-interviews-optimize-for-iteration-surma-dev-spzhrflx6","summary":"I recently went through a interviews at a couple of companies to eventually land my new gig at Shopify. Afterwards, I spent some time thinking how I evaluated candidates as an interviewer and how I approached my technical interview questions as a candidate. I realized that there\u2019s probably some experience worth sharing, hence this blog post.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/6d72f35beded8ee96f9ada70e161cf54","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-01-24T15:33:18.807Z"},{"id":"57LpPeDkM","title":"<video>, HTTP range requests & WHATWG streams \u2014 surma.dev","url":"https://surma.dev/things/range-requests/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/video-http-range-requests-whatwg-streams-surma-dev-57lppedkm","summary":"I\u2019m working on my backup server and want to use Perkeep as one of my main data stores. Perkeep stores your data as chunk of bytes called blobs. Each blob is content-addressable, meaning that each blob is identified by its SHA224 hash. Since the parts are listed in order, it also opens up the possibility of streaming the file contents.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/3ee47f5bb320cbc06fca0f2e279bf6df","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2021-12-28T05:24:35.672Z"},{"id":"o3D01cHju","title":"Is WebAssembly magic performance pixie dust?","url":"https://surma.dev/things/js-to-asc/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/is-webassembly-magic-performance-pixie-dust--o3d01chju","summary":"WebAssembly and JavaScript have the same peak performance. Given ideal conditions, they both compile to machine code and end up being equally fast. I think it would be better if we thought about WebAssembly as a way to get more reliable performance. There are also some other qualities of WebAssembly that might make it better suited in specific situations than JavaScript.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/beecd4f7d6e5334696cd1ea3ff416872","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2021-04-13T00:00:00.000Z"}],"similar_handles":["lethain","metabase","atti","komodor","curiosum"],"opposite_handles":["felixrieseberg","hamelhusain","xai","hwchase17","sama"],"similar":[{"id":"lethain","handle":"lethain","name":"Irrational Exuberance","is_squad":false,"x":-4.2839,"y":3.4323,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":174,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/e6ab29f02f344049b087fabd480dcaf0","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":0.979754,"median_upvotes":1.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"hype_score":0.005747,"avg_read_time":7.511494,"tag_diversity":0.54023},"top_tags_preview":[["leadership",49],["llm",28],["ai",21]],"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[-0.3382,6.6324],"cadence_depth":[2.4118,3.2353],"hype_variety":[-0.8824,5.8824],"title_style":[8.0294,6.5147]}},{"id":"metabase","handle":"metabase","name":"Metabase","is_squad":false,"x":-4.3027,"y":3.4948,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected"